        "manifest": {
          "title": "The ball stops rising. Gravity does not stop.",
          "summary": "A ball tossed straight up rises, is still for an instant at the top and falls back, on a fixed height scale. A blue Motion arrow follows its velocity while a warm Gravity arrow stays the same downward length throughout.",
          "assumptions": [
            "Gravity fixed at 9.8 m/s^2, no air resistance, up is positive."
          ],
          "description": "A ball moves straight up from a launch-height line beside a fixed vertical height scale in metres, then falls back to the line. A blue Motion arrow beside the ball shrinks as it rises, disappears at the top and points down as it falls. A warm Gravity arrow on the other side always points down with the same length. A callout next to the ball names its motion and states that gravity pulls down.",
